  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial phase one budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project has progressed through several stages: initial findings in August suggested a 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms; a call for ideas in July focused on AI-enhanced data visualization; strategic partnerships with TechInnovate were explored and secured to leverage AI research; a training budget of $15,000 was approved for coding teams and project managers; a significant milestone was reached with the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th; and phase two progress in November highlighted breakthroughs in predictive analytics. Currently, feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
